From decdc0ceba3e1689019164995b3f5d09d36a4251 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soulexit <metehan.tanriverdi01@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:43:26 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 64/69] panvk, pan/kmod: build fixes after the Mesa 27 merge

- kbase backend: stub util_sync_provider (kbase uses panvk's CPU sync
  type), pan_kmod_dev_init() argument order.
- pan_kmod: keep the panfrost backend entry under its #if.
- panvk_priv_bo_create() takes a label; set it after
  panvk_priv_bo_create_kind() and pass NULL from our callers.
- Restore indirect_info.varying_bufs (JM indirect varying buffer kept).
- pan_compile_inputs has no gpu_id any more: read it from the physical
  device for the IDVS product check; drop the unused gpu_id argument of
  pan_nir_lower_vs_inputs_poly().
- kbase pan_get_model() call with core count and features; one
  core_count in the DRM init path; u_cpu_detect.h in u_queue.c;
  arch instead of gpu_id in pan_nir_lower_tex.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
